# MicroPython QSTR / generated-header workflow

NEVER hand-edit the generated headers in `lib/micropython/micropython_embed/genhdr/`
(`qstrdefs.generated.h`, `root_pointers.h`, `moduledefs.h`). No computing QSTR
hashes by hand, ever.

Instead:

1. Add new QSTR references, `MP_REGISTER_ROOT_POINTER`, or `MP_REGISTER_MODULE`
   entries to the host-scanned source-of-truth files:
   - `lib/micropython/port/rp2_qstr_stub.c` (rp2/pin/peripheral QSTRs, root pointers)
   - `lib/micropython/port/modmachine_jl.inc` (`jl_qstr_refs()`)
2. Run `scripts/build_micropython.sh` to regenerate `micropython_embed/` from the
   pinned MicroPython checkout in `micropython_repo/`. It prints a QSTR diff vs
   the previous build — verify your new QSTRs show up as added.

Also remember: `lib/micropython/port/*.c|h` files are copied into
`lib/micropython/micropython_embed/port/` (both copies compile and link with
`--allow-multiple-definition`). Edit the `port/` copy and re-run the build
script — or `cp` manually — so the two never diverge.
